    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10282" root="خرج" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرْجَةٌ</span></b>  [n. un. of 1: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرَجَاتٌ</span>]. You say,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا خَرَجَ إِلَّا خَرْجَةً وَاحِدَةً</span> <i>He went not,</i> or <i>came not,
out,</i> or <i>forth, save once:</i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَكْثَرَ خَرَجَاتِكَ</span>
<i>How many are thy goings,</i> or <i>comings, out,</i> or
<i>forth!</i> (A.)

